{"name":"Bathing Beauty","hex":"#428267","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bathing beauty","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An attractive woman in a bathing suit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bathing_beauty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bathing Beauty","blocks":[{"text":"Bathing Beauty is a 1944 American musical romantic comedy film directed by George Sidney and starring Red Skelton and Esther Williams."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Bathing_Beauty_%281944_film_poster%29.png/330px-Bathing_Beauty_%281944_film_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathing_Beauty","wikidata":"Q2698019"},{"title":"Bathing","blocks":[{"text":"Bathing is the immersion of the body, wholly or partially, usually in water, but often in another medium such as hot air. It is most commonly practised as part of personal cleansing, and less frequently for relaxation or as a leisure activity. Cleansing the body may be solely a component of personal hygiene, but is also a spiritual part of some religious rituals. Bathing is also sometimes used medically or therapeutically, as in hydrotherapy, ice baths, or the mud bath."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Norblin_Bath_in_the_park_%28detail%29_02.jpg/330px-Norblin_Bath_in_the_park_%28detail%29_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bathing","wikidata":"Q327651"},{"title":"Beauty","blocks":[{"text":"Beauty is commonly described as a feature of objects that makes them pleasurable to perceive. Such objects include landscapes, sunsets, humans and works of art. Beauty, art and taste are the main subjects of aesthetics, one of the fields of study within philosophy. As a positive aesthetic value, it is contrasted with ugliness as its negative counterpart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg/330px-Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beauty","wikidata":"Q7242"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/Bathingbeauty-waterballet2.jpg/330px-Bathingbeauty-waterballet2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/Bathingbeauty-waterballet2.jpg/330px-Bathingbeauty-waterballet2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Esther Williams emerges from the water during the finale.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABathingbeauty-waterballet2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/500px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/1280px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg/500px-Showering_on_Skylab_%289456594881%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Astronaut Jack R. Lousma taking a shower in space, 1973","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShowering_on_Skylab_(9456594881).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg/500px-A_woman_preparing_to_bathe._Gouache_painting._Wellcome_V0019991.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/A_woman_preparing_